    "spans": [
     {
      "end": 531,
      "start": 0,
      "text": "Martin Behaim\nMartin Behaim ( 6 October 1459 -- 29 July 1507 ) , also known as and by various forms of ( Martinus Bohemus and de Bo\u00ebmia ; Martinho da Bo\u00e9mia Martin Behaim von Schwarzbach ) was a German mariner , artist , cosmographer , astronomer , philosopher , geographer , and explorer in service to King John II . His maps are sometimes held to have been influential on the Age of Discovery but he is now best known for his Erdapfel , the world 's oldest surviving globe , which he produced for the Imperial City of Nuremberg ."
     }
    ],
    "status": "ok"
   },
